					"properties": {
						"text": "[color=E25A12]Alex:[/color]\n\n[color=989DB1]You speak to desiring a perfect finished work, but I see you uniquely title each draft that paves the way towards that end. What is the importance of these drafts versus your finished paintings once you've moved on from them? [/color]\n\n[color=50A359]Sean:[/color]\n\n[color=989DB1]I mostly create work in progress pieces for when I make an important decision which heavily alters a painting, or if I want to share a draft to the No Paint Discord server. I find those drafts important because that is how I can remember the way I created my work.[color=E25A12]",
